Composite the Linux web view on the GPU.

JUCE 8.0.14's WebKitGTK backend sets the hardware acceleration policy to
"never", so WebKit rasterises and composites every frame on the CPU. WebView2
(Windows) and WKWebView (macOS) both composite on the GPU, so on the same
machine the Linux build's animations, transitions and backdrop filters run
visibly slower: a backdrop blur is re-rendered in software on every frame
behind it.

Use "always" instead. JUCE's choice was probably a cautious one, since the view
runs in a forked GTK child that is embedded over XEmbed and forced onto the
X11 backend (XWayland on a Wayland session), and some drivers do not composite
there. So keep that choice one environment variable away:
PLECTRIFY_WEBKIT_SOFTWARE_RENDERING=1 restores "never". The forked child
inherits the parent's environment, so setting it where Plectrify is launched
is enough.

diff --git a/modules/juce_gui_extra/native/juce_WebBrowserComponent_linux.cpp b/modules/juce_gui_extra/native/juce_WebBrowserComponent_linux.cpp
--- a/modules/juce_gui_extra/native/juce_WebBrowserComponent_linux.cpp
+++ b/modules/juce_gui_extra/native/juce_WebBrowserComponent_linux.cpp
@@ -805,10 +805,20 @@ public:
 
         auto* settings = wk.juce_webkit_settings_new();
 
+        // PLECTRIFY_WEBKIT_GPU: composite on the GPU, as WebView2 and WKWebView
+        // do. JUCE hard-codes "never", which rasterises every frame on the CPU
+        // and makes animations and backdrop filters crawl. Setting
+        // PLECTRIFY_WEBKIT_SOFTWARE_RENDERING=1 restores JUCE's choice for a
+        // driver that cannot composite inside the embedded X11 window.
+        static constexpr int webkitHadwareAccelerationPolicyAlwaysFlag = 1;
         static constexpr int webkitHadwareAccelerationPolicyNeverFlag = 2;
 
+        const auto* softwareRendering = std::getenv ("PLECTRIFY_WEBKIT_SOFTWARE_RENDERING");
+        const auto forceSoftware = softwareRendering != nullptr && std::strcmp (softwareRendering, "1") == 0;
+
         WebKitSymbols::getInstance()->juce_webkit_settings_set_hardware_acceleration_policy (settings,
-                                                                                             webkitHadwareAccelerationPolicyNeverFlag);
+                                                                                             forceSoftware ? webkitHadwareAccelerationPolicyNeverFlag
+                                                                                                           : webkitHadwareAccelerationPolicyAlwaysFlag);
         if (initialisationData->userAgent.isNotEmpty())
             WebKitSymbols::getInstance()->juce_webkit_settings_set_user_agent (settings,
                                                                                initialisationData->userAgent.toRawUTF8());
